Arborescence","identifier":"doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/Arborescence","url":"\/documentation\/trees\/arborescence","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An arborescence: a directed tree whose edges all point away from its root, so every vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"but the root has exactly one incoming edge, from its parent. As a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"successors(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" are the children, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"predecessors(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" is the parent (zero or one), and each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edge is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedEdge(from: parent, to: child)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"topic"}}}